    "21:1–9 — Then there was a famine in the days of David three years, year after year; and David enquired of the LORD. And the LORD answered, It is for Saul, and for his bloody house, because he slew the Gibeonites. And the king called the Gibeonites. What shall I do for you? and wherewith shall I make the atonement, that ye may bless the inheritance of the LORD? And they said, The man that consumed us, let seven men of his sons be delivered unto us, and we will hang them up unto the LORD in Gibeah of Saul. And the king said, I will give them. But the king spared Mephibosheth, because of the LORD’s oath between David and Jonathan. But the king took the two sons of Rizpah, and the five sons of Michal the daughter of Saul, whom she brought up for Adriel. And he delivered them unto the Gibeonites, and they hanged them in the hill before the LORD: and they fell all seven together in the beginning of barley harvest. Three hungry years before anyone asks. Joshua’s Gibeon-oath, broken by Saul offstage. Seven grandsons. A different oath keeps Jonathan’s son. The land’s calendar under a grim covering.",
